CLASS:: Foa512Matrix
summary:: First Order Ambisonic (FOA) decoder matrix for 5.1.2 speaker layout
categories:: Libraries>Ambisonic Toolkit>Matrix & Kernel>FOA
related:: Classes/FoaDecoderMatrix, Classes/FoaDecode, Classes/Foa512Matrix

DESCRIPTION::
Foa512Matrix generates decoder matrices for converting FOA B-format (W, X, Y, Z) to a 5.1.2 speaker layout: 5 lower ring speakers (FL, FR, C, RL, RR), 2 height speakers (TFL, TFR), and an LFE channel.

The decoder supports three lower-ring modes (Equal, Focus, Four) and dynamically calculates height speaker coefficients based on adjustable elevation angle. Height matrix design emphasizes ambient/upper-hemisphere content while preserving spatial width.

This implementation matches the ATK JSFX plugin "5.1.2 Matrix Decode" and is designed to work seamlessly with the ATK framework.

note:: This decoder provides matrix coefficients only. The matrix outputs 7 channels (5 lower ring + 2 height). LFE is derived separately by summing FL+FR with a lowpass filter (~120 Hz) and gain boost (+10 dB). Height HPF, height gate/trim, and output routing must be handled separately in the application layer.::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Create a new Foa512Matrix instance.

argument:: mode
Lower ring decode mode:
strong::\equal:: - Balanced distribution (default)
strong::\focus:: - Emphasizes centre channel for dialogue
strong::\four:: - Eliminates centre, emphasizing corner speakers

argument:: heightElevation
Elevation angle for height speakers in degrees (30-90, default 45).

argument:: outputLayout
Output channel ordering:
strong::\uhjpi:: - FL, FR, C, RL, RR, LFE, TFL, TFR (default)
strong::\dolby:: - FL, FR, C, LFE, RL, RR, TFL, TFR

returns:: A Foa512Matrix instance.

discussion::
The matrix is calculated once on initialization. Use the elevation and mode setters to update dynamically.

code::
// Create decoder with defaults (Equal mode, 45° elevation)
decoder = Foa512Matrix.new;

// Create with Focus mode and 60° elevation
decoder = Foa512Matrix.new(\focus, 60);

// Dolby layout output
decoder = Foa512Matrix.new(\equal, 45, \dolby);
::

METHOD:: newFoaDecoder
Create a standard ATK FoaDecoderMatrix instance compatible with link::Classes/FoaDecode::.

argument:: mode
Lower ring decode mode (\equal, \focus, \four, default \equal).

argument:: heightElevation
Elevation angle for height speakers in degrees (default 45).

returns:: A link::Classes/FoaDecoderMatrix:: instance that can be used with link::Classes/FoaDecode::.

discussion::
This method wraps the Foa512Matrix matrix coefficients into an ATK-standard FoaDecoderMatrix, making it compatible with the standard ATK decoding chain.

code::
// Basic usage with FoaDecode
(
var decoder = Foa512Matrix.newFoaDecoder(\equal, 45);
var input = [W, X, Y, Z]; // B-format input
var output = FoaDecode.ar(input, decoder);
// output is 7-channel array [FL, FR, C, RL, RR, TFL, TFR]
// (LFE must be extracted separately)
)

// Different modes
var decoderEqual = Foa512Matrix.newFoaDecoder(\equal, 45);
var decoderFocus = Foa512Matrix.newFoaDecoder(\focus, 45);
var decoderFour = Foa512Matrix.newFoaDecoder(\four, 45);

// Adjustable elevation
var decoder30deg = Foa512Matrix.newFoaDecoder(\equal, 30); // Forward
var decoder90deg = Foa512Matrix.newFoaDecoder(\equal, 90); // Overhead
::

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: matrix
Get the full 7x4 decoder matrix (5 lower ring + 2 height speakers).

returns:: A Matrix object with 7 rows (speakers) and 4 columns (W, X, Y, Z coefficients).

METHOD:: elevation
Set height speaker elevation angle and recalculate height matrix.

argument:: deg
Elevation angle in degrees (30-90).

METHOD:: mode
Set lower ring decode mode and recalculate lower ring matrix.

argument:: mode
\equal, \focus, or \four.

code::
// Create decoder and adjust parameters
decoder = Foa512Matrix.new;
decoder.elevation_(60);  // Change to 60° elevation
decoder.mode_(\focus);    // Switch to Focus mode
::

METHOD:: decode
Decode B-format input to 7 output channels (lower ring + heights, no LFE).

argument:: w
W component (omnidirectional).

argument:: x
X component (left-right).

argument:: y
Y component (front-back).

argument:: z
Z component (elevation).

returns:: Array of 7 signals [FL, FR, C, RL, RR, TFL, TFR].

discussion::
This is a convenience method for manual decoding. For real-time use with full processing, implement the post-processing chain separately: LFE is created by summing FL+FR, applying a one-pole lowpass filter (~120 Hz), and adding +10 dB gain. Height channels require HPF (~80 Hz default), envelope gating (optional), and trim controls. Output routing must map decoded channels to physical outputs based on layout (UHJ-Pi vs Dolby).

EXAMPLES::

code::
// Basic decoder creation and matrix inspection
(
var decoder = Foa512Matrix.new;
decoder.matrix.postln;  // View the 7x4 matrix
decoder.printOn(Post);  // Print decoder info
)

// Use with ATK FoaDecode
(
s.boot;
{
    var w, x, y, z;
    var decoder;
    var decoded;
    
    // Test B-format input
    w = WhiteNoise.ar(0.1);
    x = SinOsc.ar(440) * 0.1;
    y = SinOsc.ar(880) * 0.1;
    z = SinOsc.ar(1320) * 0.1;
    
    // Create 5.1.2 decoder
    decoder = Foa512Matrix.newFoaDecoder(\equal, 45);
    
    // Decode using ATK
    decoded = FoaDecode.ar([w, x, y, z], decoder);
    
    // Output 7 channels (LFE must be added separately)
    Out.ar(0, decoded);
}.play;
)

// Compare different modes
(
var modes = [\equal, \focus, \four];
var decoders = modes.collect({ |m| Foa512Matrix.newFoaDecoder(m, 45) });
decoders.do({ |d| d.printOn(Post); "\n".post });
)

// Elevation sweep (requires GUI control for real-time)
(
var decoder = Foa512Matrix.new(\equal, 45);
fork {
    30.to(90).do({ |deg|
        decoder.elevation_(deg);
        ("Elevation: " ++ deg).postln;
        0.1.wait;
    });
};
)
::
